  "body": "* ```<main>``` is the **\"main\"** sectioning root. It would be good for its role and visually designing main contents (for instance, using css grid).\r\n* ```<header>```, ```<aside>```, ```<footer>```, and ```<nav>``` are additional sectioning roots. These can have sectioning content.\r\n* Other flow elements are nonsense to have ```<h#>``` because it is useless or already have one comparable to that (like ```<legend>```, ```<caption>``` etc.).\r\n* ```<section>```, and ```<article>``` remain sectioning content.\r\n* **One sectioning [root | content], one child heading.** (1)\r\n* Remove ```<hgroup>```.\r\n* *Optional*: define ```role=\"subheading\"``` ([original idea from Steve Faulkner](https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-html/2011Apr/0147.html)) and maybe reconsider ```<h>```.\r\n\r\n(1)\r\n```html\r\n<!-- this make sense -->\r\n<section>\r\n    <h1></h1>\r\n    <section>\r\n        <h1></h1>\r\n    </section>\r\n    .........\r\n</section>\r\n\r\n<!-- this is nonsense -->\r\n<section>\r\n    <h1></h1>\r\n    <h1></h1>(x)\r\n    .........\r\n</section>\r\n```",
